.TH "GENI\-UPLOADER\-AUTH\-URL" "1" "October 2026" "geni-uploader 1.0.0" "Geni Uploader Manual"
.SH NAME
geni\-uploader\-auth\-url \- generate the Geni OAuth authorization URL
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B geni\-uploader auth\-url
.BI "\-\-client\-id " "CLIENT_ID"
.BI "[\-\-redirect\-uri " "REDIRECT_URI]"
.SH DESCRIPTION
Prints the Geni OAuth authorization URL for your Geni application. Open the URL in a browser, authorize the app, and complete the desktop flow to obtain an access token. This command performs no Geni writes.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI "\-\-token\-file " "TOKEN_FILE"
file outside the repo holding the access token (global, before the command)
.TP
.BI "\-\-client\-id " "CLIENT_ID"
your Geni app's client ID (required)
.TP
.BI "\-\-redirect\-uri " "REDIRECT_URI"
only if your app settings define a callback URL; the desktop flow (default) needs none
.TP
.B \-\-help
Show a short summary and the option list, then exit.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B geni\-uploader auth\-url \-\-client\-id 12345
Print the authorization URL for the desktop OAuth flow.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
the command completed
.TP
.B 1
failure (see the diagnostic log)
.TP
.B 2
refused (for example a missing \-\-confirm YES)
.TP
.B 3
uncertain items remain; review them on Geni before re\-running
.TP
.B 4
identity or tag verification stopped the run
.TP
.B 5
uploads are verified on Geni; only the repository status push failed
.TP
.B 6
another run holds the state lock
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR geni\-uploader (1).
